# DDC/CI panel control (feral-controld drives ddcutil for brightness, contrast,
# volume, power and the panel status poll) needs read/write on the GPU's
# /dev/i2c-* buses.
#
# The ddcutil package grants those buses with TAG+="uaccess" in
# /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-ddcutil-i2c.rules. uaccess is an ACL that
# systemd-logind applies for the user of the ACTIVE SEAT SESSION only. That
# worked while feralfile logged in through the tty1 autologin getty. Since
# ffos#126 nothing logs in: the kiosk, watchdog and controld run inside
# user@1000 (started by linger) with no logind session at all, so no ACL is
# ever applied, /dev/i2c-* stays root:root 0600 and every ddcutil call fails
# with EACCES. cage is unaffected because it reaches DRM through seatd.
#
# So grant the buses to group i2c instead (feralfile is a member; the group is
# pre-seeded in etc/group and re-applied by the install/OTA scripts). Same
# device match as the ddcutil rule (I2C buses whose PCI parent is a display
# controller), which is the match that provably worked on FF1 hardware before
# ffos#126; other I2C/SMBus buses stay root-only. This file is additive to the
# package rule (61 > 60), so a ddcutil upgrade cannot silently replace it.
# docs/BOOT_DISPLAY_AND_CONSOLE.md rule 6 and scripts/verify.sh pin it.
SUBSYSTEM=="i2c-dev", KERNEL=="i2c-[0-9]*", ATTRS{class}=="0x03*", GROUP="i2c", MODE="0660"
